🧩 Main Components and Where to Change Each Rule
1. JiraFlowCoordinator

Main orchestration class

This is the central entry point of the integration. It coordinates the complete Jira publishing flow and prepares all execution context before any Jira request is sent.

Responsible for

• storing the main integration configuration
• defining base values such as Jira URL, project key, Epic key, labels, environment, and file names
• resolving the correct report folder
• identifying the suite name from the report path
• generating the execution summary
• generating the Test Plan name
• locating the XML result file
• collecting failure image candidates
• creating the full import flow through jiraImport()
• calling the report builder, Test Plan manager, and execution publisher in the correct order

Change this file when you need to

• update Jira base configuration
• change project key, Epic key, token usage, labels, or environment
• change how the suite name is extracted
• change how execution names are built
• change how Test Plan names are built
• change which XML report file has priority
• change how the report folder is resolved
• change the overall order of the integration flow

Key methods

• jiraImport()
• getResolvedReportFolder()
• getCurrentSuiteName()
• getExecutionSummary()
• getTestPlanName()
• findXmlFile()

