🔄 End to End Flow
Current execution flow
1. Start the flow

The process begins in JiraFlowCoordinator.jiraImport().

2. Resolve the report folder

The integration tries multiple strategies to identify the correct report folder.

3. Detect the suite name

The suite name is extracted from the resolved report folder structure.

4. Find the XML result file

The flow looks for the preferred XML file and uses fallback logic when necessary.

5. Collect failure images

Potential evidence files are collected from the report structure.

6. Generate the GAIA HTML report

JiraGaiaReportBuilder creates gaiaReport.html.

7. Resolve the Test Plan

JiraTestPlanManager decides whether to reuse an existing Test Plan or create a new one.

8. Import execution results into Jira

JiraGateway.importExecutionResults() sends the XML result file.

9. Link execution to the Test Plan

JiraGateway.addExecutionToTestPlan() associates the execution with the chosen Test Plan.

10. Update execution metadata

JiraGateway.updateTestExecution() updates summary, labels, and environment.

11. Package execution artifacts

JiraExecutionPublisher creates Results.zip and Evidences.zip.

12. Upload attachments

The generated report and ZIP files are uploaded to the Jira Test Execution.

